  'Propanone reacts with CH3MgBr, then H3O+, to give A; A is dehydrated with conc. H2SO4 to give B; B is ozonised (O3 then Zn/H2O). The products are|propanone and methanal|ethanal and methanal|propanal and methanal|propanone and ethanal|4|A is 2-methylpropan-2-ol; dehydration gives 2-methylpropene (B); ozonolysis gives (CH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>2</sub>C=O and HCHO.',
